{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall not.</b> If you see many testify about a matter you do not know, do not say in your heart, \"These cannot lie.\" The Gaon [Saadia] said that there are two commandments in this verse: one a negative commandment and the second a positive commandment, for he said you are obligated אחרי רבים להטות (to follow the majority), because he thought that the word להטות is like לנטות, but it is not so. Rather, it is of the heavy dagesh construction, like ארור מטה משפט (Deuteronomy 27:19). It is also found without משפט: ומטי גר (Malachi 3:5). And the Sages of blessed memory explained that from this we learn that the halakhah follows the majority, and what they transmitted is the truth. And since Scripture said לא תהיה אחרי רבים לרעות, from this we learn that if the majority are for good — which is a commandment — one follows them." "<b>You shall not testify in a dispute.</b> A commandment upon all Israel, and even the judge who has the dispute brought before him — to help his fellow."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Resolved חז\"ל as 'the Sages of blessed memory' per standard convention."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:33.471726775Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}